# Copy to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is gitignored; never commit it.
#
# Always run with the `env -u` prefix so this file wins over stale shell exports:
#
#   env -u ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -u ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN -u ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL \
#       -u OPENAI_API_KEY -u OPENAI_BASE_URL -u CODEX_HOME -u CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR \
#       uv run --env-file .env --locked assembly-world-agent run ...

# --- Claude Code ---

# Anthropic API key. Takes precedence over the subscription login.
# Leave empty to use the subscription login in CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Claude Code config and credential directory. Always point this at a dedicated
# directory, one per identity, so the credential an experiment uses is
# unambiguous:
#   - API key identity: an empty directory, no login. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is then
#     the only credential and `claude auth status` reports authMethod=api_key.
#   - subscription identity: run `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<dir> claude auth login` once.
# Two traps. An empty value is read as an empty path, so Claude Code writes its
# state into the working directory. And the default `~/.claude` may already hold
# a subscription login that reports authMethod=claude.ai even when
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set, which silently changes what a run bills against.
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=$HOME/.claude-awa-api

# Bearer token. Ranks above ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Unused here.
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Anthropic API base URL. Unused here; official endpoint only.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# --- Codex ---

# Codex config and credential directory. The only working identity switch,
# because `auth.json` holds one auth mode at a time. One directory per identity:
#   CODEX_HOME=$HOME/.codex-awa-sub codex login
#   printenv OPENAI_API_KEY | CODEX_HOME=$HOME/.codex-awa-api codex login --with-api-key
CODEX_HOME=

# OpenAI API key. Only for the one-time `codex login --with-api-key` above.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# OpenAI API base URL. Verified to have no effect under a ChatGPT login. For a
# third-party or local OpenAI-compatible endpoint pass `--codex-config` overrides to
# `run` instead (see README).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# --- OpenRouter through Codex ---

# Full Authorization header value for an OpenRouter run. Codex 0.154 does not send
# `env_key`, so the run passes
# `--codex-config 'model_providers.openrouter.env_http_headers={Authorization="OPENROUTER_AUTH"}'`
# and this variable is copied into the header verbatim; only the variable name
# reaches the command line and run.json.
# OPENROUTER_AUTH="Bearer sk-or-v1-..."
